#: tfrmpointerscannersettings.btnok.caption
msgctxt "tfrmpointerscannersettings.btnok.caption"
msgid "OK"
msgstr "OK"

#: tfrmpointerscannersettings.caption
msgid "Pointerscanner scanoptions"
msgstr "ポインタスキャナスキャンオプション"

#: tfrmpointerscannersettings.cbacceptnonmodulevtable.caption
msgid "Also accept non-module addresses"
msgstr "非モジュールアドレスも受け入れる"

#: tfrmpointerscannersettings.cballigned.caption
msgid "Addresses must be 32-bit alligned"
msgstr "アドレスは 32ビットアライン必須"

#: tfrmpointerscannersettings.cballigned.hint
msgid ""
"When enabled, only pointers that are stored in an address dividable by 4 are "
"looked at\n"
"When disabled, it won't bother.\n"
"\n"
"pro: Fast scans\n"
"Con: On some horrible designed games that you shouldn't even play it won't find "
"the paths\n"
msgstr ""

#: tfrmpointerscannersettings.cballowruntimeworkers.caption
msgid "Allow scanners to connect at runtime"
msgstr "実行時のスキャナ接続を許可"

#: tfrmpointerscannersettings.cballowruntimeworkers.hint
msgid ""
"Opens a port that other systems running the pointerscanner can connect to and "
"help out with the scan"
msgstr "ポインタスキャナを実行している他のシステムが接続してスキャンを支援できるポートを開きます"

#: tfrmpointerscannersettings.cbclasspointersonly.caption
msgid "First element of pointerstruct must point to module (e.g vtable)"
msgstr "ポインタ構造体の最初の要素はモジュールを指す必要があります(例：vtable)"

#: tfrmpointerscannersettings.cbclasspointersonly.hint
msgid ""
"Object oriented programming languages tend to implement classobjects by having "
"a pointer in the first element to something that describes the class\n"
"With this option enabled, ce will check if it's a classobject by checking that "
"rule. If not, it won't see it as a pointer.\n"
"pro:Tremendous speed increase and almost perfect pointers\n"
"con:Doesn't work with runtime generated classes (java, .net) \n"
msgstr ""

#: tfrmpointerscannersettings.cbcomparetootherpointermaps.caption
msgid "Compare results with other saved pointermap(s)"
msgstr "結果を他の保存済みポインタマップと比較"

#: tfrmpointerscannersettings.cbcomparetootherpointermaps.hint
msgid ""
"When ticked you can add other pointermaps which will be used to verify that the "
"pointers it finds are correct. You will have to fill in the correct address for "
"each pointermap you provide.\n"
"Note: expect at least the size of the game itself in memory for every "
"pointermap used\n"
msgstr "チェックすると、見つかったポインタが正しいことを検証するために使用される他のポインタマップを追加できます。提供する各ポインタマップに正しいアドレスを入力する必要があります。\n注意：使用するポインタマップごとに、少なくともゲーム自体のメモリサイズが必要です\n"

#: tfrmpointerscannersettings.cbcompressedpointerscanfile.caption
msgid "Compressed pointerscan file"
msgstr "圧縮ポインタスキャンファイル"

#: tfrmpointerscannersettings.cbcompressedpointerscanfile.hint
msgid ""
"Compresses the generated .PTR files slightly so they take less space on the "
"disk and less time writing to disk.\n"
"Most of the time the bottleneck of a pointerscan is disk writing, so it is "
"recommended to use this option.\n"
"\n"
"Compressed .PTR files can not be read out by older Cheat Engine versions\n"
msgstr ""

#: tfrmpointerscannersettings.cbconnecttonode.caption
msgid "Connect to pointerscan node"
msgstr "ポインタスキャンノードに接続"

#: tfrmpointerscannersettings.cbconnecttonode.hint
msgid ""
"When checked will send a broadcast message on the local network which will tell "
"pointer scanner systems to join this scan if they are set to auto join\n"
"\n"
"You can use \"Setup specific IP's to notify\" to notify systems of this scan "
"that are outside of the local network\n"
msgstr ""

#: tfrmpointerscannersettings.cbheaponly.caption
msgid "Only allow static and heap addresses in the path"
msgstr "パス内の静的アドレスとヒープアドレスのみを許可"

#: tfrmpointerscannersettings.cbheaponly.hint
msgid ""
"If the address you search for isn't a heap address, the scan will return 0 "
"results"
msgstr "検索するアドレスがヒープアドレスでない場合、スキャン結果は0になります"

#: tfrmpointerscannersettings.cbincludesystemmodules.caption
msgctxt "tfrmpointerscannersettings.cbincludesystemmodules.caption"
msgid "Include system modules"
msgstr "システムモジュールを含める"

#: tfrmpointerscannersettings.cblimitscantoregionfile.caption
msgctxt "tfrmpointerscannersettings.cblimitscantoregionfile.caption"
msgid "Limit scan to specified region file"
msgstr "スキャンを指定領域ファイルに制限"

#: tfrmpointerscannersettings.cbmaxoffsetspernode.caption
msgid "Max different offsets per node:"
msgstr "ノードごとの最大異なるオフセット数："

#: tfrmpointerscannersettings.cbmaxoffsetspernode.hint
msgid ""
"When the pointerscan looks through the list of pointers with a specific value, "
"it goes through every single pointer that has that value. Every time increasing "
"the offset slightly.\n"
"With this feature enabled the pointerscan will only check the first few "
"pointers with that value.\n"
"\n"
"pro: Extremely fast, and the results have the lowest pointer paths possible.\n"
"con: You'll miss a lot of pointers that might be valid too \n"
msgstr ""

#: tfrmpointerscannersettings.cbmustendwithspecificoffset.caption
msgid "Pointers must end with specific offsets"
msgstr "ポインタは特定のオフセットで終わる必要があります"

#: tfrmpointerscannersettings.cbmuststartwithbase.caption
msgid "Base address must be in specific range"
msgstr "ベースアドレスは特定の範囲内である必要があります"

#: tfrmpointerscannersettings.cbmuststartwithbase.hint
msgid ""
"Will only mark the given range as valid base address (Will reduce the number of "
"results)\n"
"This internally makes use of the \"Only find paths with a static address\" "
"feature by marking the provided range as static only, so it must be enabled.\n"
msgstr ""

#: tfrmpointerscannersettings.cbnegativeoffsets.caption
msgid "Also scan for negative offsets"
msgstr "負のオフセットもスキャン"

#: tfrmpointerscannersettings.cbnegativeoffsets.hint
msgid ""
"Let's you scan for negative offsets\n"
"Can not be used in combination with compressed pointerscan files\n"
msgstr ""

#: tfrmpointerscannersettings.cbnoloop.caption
msgid "No looping pointers"
msgstr "ループするポインタを除外"

#: tfrmpointerscannersettings.cbnoloop.hint
msgid ""
"This will filter out pointerpaths that ended up in a loop\n"
"e.g:\n"
"base->p1->p2->p3->p1->p4\n"
"\n"
"you could just as well do base->p1->p4 then, so throw this one away (base->p1-"
">p4 will be found another way)\n"
"\n"
"pro: Less results so less diskspace used\n"
"con: slightly slows down the scan as it needs to check for loops every single "
"iteration \n"
msgstr ""

#: tfrmpointerscannersettings.cbnoreadonly.caption
msgid "Don't include pointers with read-only nodes"
msgstr "読み取り専用ノードのポインタを含めない"

#: tfrmpointerscannersettings.cbnoreadonly.hint
msgid ""
"When checked the pointerscan will throw away memory that is readonly. So when "
"it looks for paths, it won't encounter paths that pass through read only memory "
"blocks.\n"
"\n"
"When it's unchecked, it does include readonly memory\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"pro: faster, less useless results\n"
"con: If the game decides to mark a pointer as readonly ce won't find it \n"
msgstr ""

#: tfrmpointerscannersettings.cbonlyonestatic.caption
msgid "Stop traversing a path when a static has been found"
msgstr "静的アドレスが見つかったらパスの探索を停止"

#: tfrmpointerscannersettings.cbonlyonestatic.hint
msgid ""
"When the pointerscanner goes through the list of pointervalues with a specific "
"value, this will stop exploring other paths as soon as it encounters a static "
"pointer to that value\n"
"\n"
"pro: Fast\n"
"con: You may miss some valid results \n"
msgstr ""

#: tfrmpointerscannersettings.cbshowadvancedoptions.caption
msgid "Show advanced options"
msgstr "詳細オプションを表示"

#: tfrmpointerscannersettings.cbstackonly.caption
msgid "Stack addresses as ONLY static address"
msgstr "スタックアドレスのみを静的アドレスとして扱う"

#: tfrmpointerscannersettings.cbstackonly.hint
msgid ""
"Enable this if you wish to only find pointer paths with a stack address.\n"
"Combine this with \"Only find paths with a static address\" (default on) else "
"this option will have no effect\n"
"\n"
"pro: You'll only get paths from the stack\n"
"con: You don't get paths from random dll's or the .exe \n"
msgstr ""

#: tfrmpointerscannersettings.cbstaticonly.caption
msgid "Only find paths with a static address"
msgstr "静的アドレスを持つパスのみ検索"

#: tfrmpointerscannersettings.cbstaticonly.hint
msgid ""
"When checked the pointerscan will only store a path when it starts with a "
"static address. (or easily looked up address)\n"
"When it's disabled, it finds every single pointer path\n"
"\n"
"pro: Fast\n"
"con: It may miss pointers that are accessed by special paths like thread local "
"storage. (but even then they'd be useless for ce as they will change)\n"
msgstr ""

#: tfrmpointerscannersettings.cbstaticstacks.caption
msgid "Allow stack addresses of the first thread(s) to be handled as static"
msgstr "最初のスレッドのスタックアドレスを静的として扱うことを許可"

#: tfrmpointerscannersettings.cbstaticstacks.hint
msgid ""
"This allows the stack of threads to be seen as static addresses by the "
"pointerscan.\n"
"The main thread is always a sure bet that it's the first one in the list. And "
"often the second thread created is pretty stable as well.\n"
"With more there's a bigger change they get created and destroyed randomly\n"
"\n"
"When a program enters a function and exits it, the stack pointer decreases and "
"increases, and the data there gets written to.\n"
"The farther the game is inside function calls, the more static the older data "
"will be.\n"
"\n"
"With max stack offset: you can set the max size that can be deemed as static "
"enough.\n"
"\n"
"pro: It finds paths otherwise never found\n"
"con: More results, more diskspace \n"
msgstr ""

#: tfrmpointerscannersettings.cbuseheapdata.caption
msgid "Improve pointerscan with gathered heap data"
msgstr "収集したヒープデータでポインタスキャンを改善"

#: tfrmpointerscannersettings.cbuseheapdata.hint
msgid ""
"When this is checked the heap is used to figure out the offset sizes, instead "
"of blindly guessing them.\n"
"pro: Greatly improve speed and a lot less useless results\n"
"con: if the game allocates gigantic chunks of heap memory, and then divides it "
"up itself, this will give wrong results.\n"
"\n"
"In other cases this will give perfect pointers \n"
msgstr ""

#: tfrmpointerscannersettings.cbuseloadedpointermap.caption
msgctxt "tfrmpointerscannersettings.cbuseloadedpointermap.caption"
msgid "Use saved pointermap"
msgstr "保存済みポインタマップを使用"

#: tfrmpointerscannersettings.cbuseloadedpointermap.hint
msgid ""
"Use this if you have created a pointermap on a system that runs the game, but "
"you wish to do the scan on another system (or multiple systems).\n"
"Checking this option will open a dialog where you can select the pointermap\n"
msgstr ""

